  "final_text": "Both objects exist and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration:** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` has `timestamp` as its time field. The fields that matter here are `response` (string codes, with a `response.keyword` subfield for exact matching), `bytes`, `clientip`, `url`, `geo.*` and `machine.*`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-1b5a53ad Web logs overview`** (id `0aa39d38-fbf7-47d7-a970-59fc24a9f569`)\n- Markdown header\n- Total requests (count)\n- Average response size (bytes)\n- Top response codes (data table)\n- Requests over time (XY line chart)\n- Requests by response code (donut)\n\n**Rule: `EFF-1b5a53ad 5xx spike`** (id `78b4067d-d833-4406-ba4d-21f253b1ca8c`)\n- Type: Elasticsearch query, consumer `stackAlerts`\n- Runs every `1m`, with a 5-minute window\n- Fires when the count is `> 10`, matching `response.keyword: 5??` (all three-digit 5xx codes)\n- Enabled, and its last execution status is `ok`\n\n**Choices I made that you may want to change:**\n- The dashboard time range is `now-1y`. I couldn't confirm when the sample data's timestamps fall, so I chose a wide window.\n- The 5xx match uses a wildcard on the string field. I couldn't list the distinct codes in the index, so I haven't confirmed which 5xx codes actually occur in the sample data.\n- Both objects were created through the Kibana API, and I read them back to confirm. I did not open them in the browser, so I haven't visually checked how the panels render.\n\nI wrote the request payloads to the scratchpad; nothing was added to the workspace.",
